# Build context hygiene for the extended OpenClaw image.
#
# plugins/lightbulb-marketplace is COPY'd wholesale into /app/dist/extensions/, and
# it carries a local node_modules for building + testing (its `openclaw`
# devDependency alone is ~460MB of plugin-SDK types). None of that belongs in
# the image: the plugin ships only its committed dist/, resolving
# openclaw/plugin-sdk and typebox from the host at /app.
#
# Scoped to plugins/ rather than a bare **/node_modules so this cannot quietly
# change what any other COPY in the Dockerfile picks up.
plugins/*/node_modules/

# Same story for the rest of each plugin's dev-only footprint: the runtime
# loader needs only dist/, openclaw.plugin.json, and package.json (its
# `openclaw.extensions`/`runtimeExtensions` fields point at dist/). src/,
# tests, lockfiles, and build/test config are committed for CI (which builds
# and tests from the git checkout, never the image) and otherwise just ride
# along dead weight — the lightbulb-channel/lightbulb-marketplace
# package-lock.json alone is ~220KB apiece.
#
# NOT excluding plugins/*/fixtures/: the build workflow's own qualify step
# runs the built image and reads
# /app/dist/extensions/lightbulb-channel/fixtures/production.json out of it
# (.github/workflows/build-openclaw-image.yml), so that fixture is a runtime
# dependency of image qualification, not a test-only artifact.
#
# NOT excluding a bare plugins/**/*.test.*: aws-exec-profile and
# paperclip-exec-creds keep their root-level index.test.mjs as a RUNTIME
# qualification asset too — the same build workflow's qualify step
# docker-runs
# `node --test /app/dist/extensions/{aws-exec-profile,paperclip-exec-creds}/index.test.mjs`
# straight from the built image, so those two files must ship. The
# plugins/*/src/ rule below already drops every *.test.ts nested under
# lightbulb-channel's/lightbulb-marketplace's src/ (their only tests,
# checkout-only), so no separate test-file pattern is needed.
plugins/*/src/
plugins/*/package-lock.json
plugins/*/tsconfig.json
plugins/*/vitest.config.ts
